From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 11:40:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve exact TileLang async-copy wait counts

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Local-base: b26f48b85790b832993f2c9d240dc3c39d6075e8, the five-patch refresh from deployment PR #875.
Upstream-source: https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang/pull/3568
Upstream-head: 8c8b68eb060af819f58b35e1b899e1e765fea918

Rationale: A same-stage consumer must wait for every committed async-copy group. Remove post-hoc wait relaxation that leaves a required group in flight.

Quality: Changes synchronization only; no arithmetic or tensor layout changes are intended. Additional waiting may alter performance, which remains unqualified for serving.

Tests: Three async pipeline transform regressions pass twice; parent control fails all three twice.
Recorded compiler tree: d3f87002969889c367e95804b1ff71dff7f11619.
See this candidate's results.json and immutable raw receipts. Full image,
retained-feature and serving qualification remain separate gates.

Upstream-status: open PR, checked 2026-11-04; pinned experimental backport.
Remove this local backport when advancing to an upstream revision containing it.
---

